+    // DEFAULT OFF: it is correct (text identical) but UNPROVEN.  At the widths this kernel actually sees -- the
+    // generation-width repeats, e.g. [2560 x 4 x 2] -- the op census shows no change (2683 vs 2671 ms), because the
+    // 89k-prefill REPEAT that costs 2622 ms (7.4 % of the op budget) is served by a FUSED window in
+    // `ggml-cuda-try-fuse.cu`, not by this dispatch.  Flip it on only with a per-width win; the prefill win has to
+    // be made inside that fusion (`RESULTS-session3.md` §11).
+    static const bool vec = [] {
